From 37cbfe591a80fbf705132012529be4ac7151d414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:49:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/23] runtime: accept mutable-format Metal swapchains so
 Godot 4 Metal apps can render

Godot 4 with the Metal rendering driver asks for its colour swapchain with
usage COLOR_ATTACHMENT | SAMPLED | MUTABLE_FORMAT (format 71,
MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Unorm_sRGB, arraySize 2) because it renders through a
view of the swapchain texture with the sibling sRGB/UNORM pixel format.
SupportedUsageFlags only whitelisted XR_SWAPCHAIN_USAGE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT
for Vulkan, so xrCreateSwapchain returned XR_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED,
Godot logged "No swapchain could be acquired to render to!" and the stream
stayed black.

Mirror the Vulkan handling for Metal: accept the bit, and when it is
requested create the swapchain textures with MTLTextureUsagePixelFormatView
so the application can make a compatible-format view (RGBA8Unorm <->
RGBA8Unorm_sRGB, BGRA8 likewise). The flag is only set on request because
Metal may disable lossless texture compression for such textures. The
runtime's own slice views keep the texture's pixel format, so the staging
textures and the encoder path are unchanged.

Tests: the Metal MUTABLE_FORMAT validation case now expects success for a
colour format and rejection for a depth format, and the runtime API test
creates and destroys a Godot-shaped Metal swapchain (format 71, arraySize 2,
mutable format).

